## Regenerating the SDK

> This section is emitted by `templates/README.mustache` (a local template
> override), so it survives regeneration. Every other section of this file is
> stock generator output and gets overwritten on every `./scripts/generate.sh`
> run. If you need to change this section, edit the template, not this file —
> a hand-edit here would be silently discarded the next time the SDK is
> regenerated, which is precisely the failure mode described below.

This SDK is a build product, not hand-written Go. The pipeline:

```
api/v3.upstream.yaml   (pristine copy of the upstream spec — never edit)
        + api/overlay.yaml  (24 reviewable corrections, each with a `reason`
                              and a `remove_when` so stale ones get noticed)
        = api/swagger.yaml  (build product of scripts/build_spec.py — never hand-edit)
        -> scripts/generate.sh (openapi-generator 7.24.0 + templates/ overrides)
        = this SDK
```

`make verify` is the gate: it regenerates the SDK from scratch and fails on
any diff between that output and what's committed. **Run it before pushing.**

```
make verify
```

Why this matters: the v2.3 SDK fixed generator defects by hand-editing the
generated `.go` files directly, and "protected" those edits with a
`.swagger-codegen-ignore` file — which the generator (openapi-generator, not
swagger-codegen) never reads. Every one of those 21 hand-patches was one
regeneration away from being silently destroyed, with no signal that it had
happened. Corrections belong in `api/overlay.yaml` (spec-level fixes) or
`templates/` (codegen-level fixes), never in the generated Go output.

The generator is pinned to exactly **7.24.0**: generated output differs
across generator versions, and the verification gate compares byte-for-byte,
so a version drift shows up as a spurious (and confusing) diff.

`go vet ./...` (bare) is expected to fail on this codebase: openapi-generator
7.24.0's `model_oneof.mustache` template has a bug that emits duplicated
if/else branches for oneOf schemas with 2+ variants, which `go vet` correctly
flags as unreachable code — except the code is generator-emitted, not a
mistake in this repo. `scripts/generate.sh` therefore runs
`go vet -unreachable=false ./...`, which is the form to use; do not
reintroduce a bare `go vet ./...` anywhere in tooling for this SDK.

There is currently no CI workflow wired up for this gate (that was a
deliberate choice, not an oversight) — `make verify` is run locally before
pushing. If CI is added later: the openapi-generator 7.24.0 CLI jar from
Maven Central
(`https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/openapitools/openapi-generator-cli/7.24.0/openapi-generator-cli-7.24.0.jar`)
is byte-identical (verified by MD5) to the jar Homebrew installs locally, and
running it directly with `java -jar openapi-generator-cli-7.24.0.jar version`
prints exactly `7.24.0` with no extra banner text — a clean way to pin the
exact version `scripts/generate.sh` checks for, without depending on the
`@openapitools/openapi-generator-cli` npm wrapper (whose own `version`
command can print extra text depending on configuration, which would break
that exact-match check).

## Installation

Import the package in a go file in your project and run `go mod tidy`:

```go
import {{packageName}} "{{gitHost}}/{{gitUserId}}/{{gitRepoId}}{{#isGoSubmodule}}/{{packageName}}{{/isGoSubmodule}}"
```

To use a proxy, set the environment variable `HTTP_PROXY`:

```go
os.Setenv("HTTP_PROXY", "http://proxy_name:proxy_port")
```

## Configuration of Server URL

Default configuration comes with `Servers` field that contains server objects as defined in the OpenAPI specification.

### Select Server Configuration

For using other server than the one defined on index 0 set context value `{{packageName}}.ContextServerIndex` of type `int`.

```go
ctx := context.WithValue(context.Background(), {{packageName}}.ContextServerIndex, 1)
```

### Templated Server URL

Templated server URL is formatted using default variables from configuration or from context value `{{packageName}}.ContextServerVariables` of type `map[string]string`.

```go
ctx := context.WithValue(context.Background(), {{packageName}}.ContextServerVariables, map[string]string{
	"basePath": "v2",
})
```

Note, enum values are always validated and all unused variables are silently ignored.

### URLs Configuration per Operation

Each operation can use different server URL defined using `OperationServers` map in the `Configuration`.
An operation is uniquely identified by `"{classname}Service.{nickname}"` string.
Similar rules for overriding default operation server index and variables applies by using `{{packageName}}.ContextOperationServerIndices` and `{{packageName}}.ContextOperationServerVariables` context maps.

```go
ctx := context.WithValue(context.Background(), {{packageName}}.ContextOperationServerIndices, map[string]int{
	"{classname}Service.{nickname}": 2,
})
ctx = context.WithValue(context.Background(), {{packageName}}.ContextOperationServerVariables, map[string]map[string]string{
	"{classname}Service.{nickname}": {
		"port": "8443",
	},
})
```

